Optional local transfer task: Inspect len without depending on iteration order. You may trace it without a Rust compiler; reading completion is not proof of a local run.

The no-argument len method returns the number of distinct stored entries. Here the repeated key updates one entry, so the map length is one; it is not the accumulated count stored at that key.
```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
fn main() {
    let mut counts: HashMap<String, u32> = HashMap::new();
    for word in ["read", "read"] {
        *counts.entry(String::from(word)).or_insert(0) += 1;
    }
    println!("{}", counts.len());
}
```
Expected output: 1.

